tion_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:f2631bd8c5379236ad7fd77455046e31064c032299f9b0484ada582912c36484","file":"preprints/A-strict-four-row-permanent-inequality-and-permutation-moments-September-26-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":14,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"04f41260a669562f06a32ec6ae4ee7d77a4664aba7bd4159eb6b4d9007af1549","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-strict-four-row-permanent-inequality-and-permutation-moments-September-26-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:f2631bd8c5379236ad7fd77455046e31064c032299f9b0484ada582912c36484","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-strict-four-row-permanent-inequality-and-permutation-moments-September-26-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L14"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"There are absolute constants $p_0\\in(4/3,2)$ and $\\varepsilon>0$ with the following property.\\label{thm:permanent} Let $\\nu$ be a probability measure on $S_4$ such that\n\\[\n \\|\\nu-u\\|_{\\TV}<\\varepsilon,\n \\qquad\n \\nu\\{\\pi:\\pi(i)=j\\}=\\frac14\\quad(1\\le i,j\\le4).\n\\]\nThen every four nonnegative functions on $\\{1,2,3,4\\}$ satisfy\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:permanent}\n \\E_\\nu\\prod_{i=1}^4f_i(\\pi(i))\\le\\prod_{i=1}^4\\|f_i\\|_{p_0}.\n\\end{equation}"}
